<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Chancellor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1556</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Chancellor was an English navigator who in 1553 sailed with Sir Hugh Willoughby's expedition in search of a north-east passage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Separated from the other ships, he reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a> and travelled overland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> received him and granted trading privileges, leading to the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscovy-company">Muscovy Company</a>. He drowned in 1556 when his ship was wrecked off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> on the return from a second voyage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-chancellor.jpg" alt="Richard Chancellor" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s Facial Chronicle (Illustrated Chronicle of Ivan the Terrible) (... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facial_Chronicle_-_b.22,_p._243_-_English_ambassadors.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
